INT. OPERA HOUSE - BALCONY BOX - EVENING

Velvet. Gilt. Below, an orchestra tunes.

CLAIRE (30s, emerald gown) sits rigid. Beside her, JACK (30s, tux, a man who bought tickets in a hurry). Two seats behind: her mother, MADAME DUBOIS (60s, pearls, lorgnette), and his father, GENERAL HARTLEY (60s, medals, mustache).

She does not look at him. He does not look at her.

Her fingers drum the armrest. His gaze stays on the stage.

The lights dim. The overture begins. His hand drifts toward hers, hesitates, withdraws. She notices.

Madame Dubois lowers her lorgnette. The General coughs.

CLAIRE
(whispering)
You came.

JACK
(whispering)
You asked.

CLAIRE
I asked in March.

JACK
I got the letter in June.

The music swells. She turns at last. He meets her eyes. The General leans forward to hear. Madame Dubois leans too.

CLAIRE
(whispering)
Stay for the second act?

JACK
(whispering)
Forever.
